{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unritual-futile-waterdogs","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Config-driven link-relation mapping (skip-not-approximate preserved)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nRelation→Jira-link mapping is hardcoded (`value_maps.RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`), and some\nrelations are deliberately unsynced (`value_maps.UNSYNCED_RELATIONS`) rather than\napproximated — the established \"skip, don't approximate\" philosophy. A Jira project whose\nconfigured link types differ (e.g. no `Supersedes`, but a `Problem/Incident` pair) has no\nconfig recourse: it can't remap a rebar relation onto the project's actual link type, nor\ndeclare a relation unsynced for that project. Link relations must become config-driven on\nthe S1 core while preserving skip-not-approximate: map to a real project link type, or\nskip — never invent an approximate link.\n\n## Approach\n\nWire the S1 `link_map` axis. Outbound: resolve the effective link map over the built-in\ndefault (`RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`); a relation mapped to a project link type uses it; a\nrelation mapped to the `skip` sentinel (or absent from the target's declared `link_types`)\nis not synced — extending, per-project, the `UNSYNCED_RELATIONS` behavior. Validation\n(S1) fails closed if a `link_map` value names a link type absent from the project's\ndeclared `link_types` vocabulary. No approximate/alternative link is ever substituted\n(that echo-unsafe path was rejected in design). Parent relationships are out of scope here\n— they are handled by S7 (drift + breadcrumb), not the link axis.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py` — built-in\n  default becomes injected fallback; resolution routed through S1.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` — link emission consults the\n  resolved map / skip set.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_link_mapping.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Config-effect contrast (unit):** with `link_map.supersedes=\"Relates\"`, an outbound\n  supersedes relation emits a `Relates` link; default leaves it unsynced — same path,\n  different config.\n- **Skip preserved:** a relation mapped to `skip` (or absent from declared `link_types`)\n  emits no link — asserted on the emitted link set.\n- **Fail-closed:** a `link_map` value naming an undeclared link type raises the named\n  validation error at load.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Effective link map = built-in ← `default` ← `projects.<KEY>`; a non-default overlay\n  changes the emitted Jira link type through the real path — verified by\n  `test_link_mapping.py::test_link_config_effect`.\n- [ ] A `skip`-mapped or undeclared relation emits no link (skip-not-approximate) —\n  verified by `test_link_mapping.py::test_link_skip_preserved`.\n- [ ] A `link_map` value naming an undeclared link type fails closed at load — verified by\n  `test_link_mapping.py::test_link_undeclared_fails_closed`.\n\nTest tier: **in-process unit** — link resolution and the emit/skip decision are pure\nfunctions; the oracle is the emitted link set and the raised validation error.","id":"1515-bebc-0d91-476b","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Config-driven link-relation mapping (skip-not-approximate preserved)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787290318169210001,"uuid":"28e504a8-9514-494a-9729-935072d72861"}